From d3ed9a7af17b77e3d449b2650d65b5d4eb13edd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 23:48:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid blocking startup on a duplicate skills refresh

The app supplies initial skill metadata asynchronously, but session
configuration also queues a blocking ListSkills command before the restored
conversation is drawn. Start the existing background refresh before initial
session projection and consume its directory ownership once. Preserve metadata
that arrives before configuration. Later configurations, changed directories,
explicit refreshes and error delivery retain their normal behavior.

Declared base: rust-v0.160.0 a956835d020762cb2b570053af06f643a11c0ecc
No downstream prerequisites; this commit touches only the TUI.

TDD RED: just test -p codex-tui -E 'test(startup_skills_refresh_)'
Both behavior tests fail on the upstream TUI: duplicate RPC and cleared
pre-configuration skill metadata. Logs: tui-red-corrected.log.
TDD GREEN: both tests pass; explicit refreshes and background errors are covered.
Full just test -p codex-tui: 5532 pass, 75 pre-existing failures, 8 skip.
Pre-fix TUI: 5530 pass, same 75 failures plus both new regressions, 8 skip.
Root just fmt-check passes. Evidence: .cat/work/reports/resume-attribution.
